 Experiment 46: To Perform Load Testing on ARMS Homepage During Peak Time by Simulating 500 Concurrent Users and Analyze Response Time, Throughput and Error Rate

 AIM
To perform load testing on the ARMS homepage using Apache JMeter by simulating 500 concurrent users and analyzing response time, throughput, and error rate.

ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter.
2. Create a new Test Plan.
3. Add a Thread Group to the Test Plan.
4. Set the number of threads (users) to 500.
5. Set the ramp-up period and loop count.
6. Add an HTTP Request Sampler.
7. Enter the ARMS homepage URL: `https://arms.srmist.edu.in/`.
8. Add Summary Report and Aggregate Report listeners.
9. Run the test and collect performance results.
10. Analyze response time, throughput, and error rate.

## PROCEDURE / CONFIGURATION

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Testing tool | Apache JMeter |
| Target website | https://arms.srmist.edu.in/ |
| Number of users | 500 |
| Ramp-up period | 100 seconds |
| Loop count | 1 |
| Request method | GET |
| Protocol | HTTPS |

## INPUT
- URL: `https://arms.srmist.edu.in/`
- Concurrent users: 500
- Ramp-up period: 100 seconds
- Loop count: 1

## OUTPUT

The following metrics are obtained from the JMeter Summary Report and Aggregate Report:

| Metric | Description |
|---|---|
| Average Response Time | Average time taken by the server to respond |
| Throughput | Number of requests processed per second |
| Error Rate | Percentage of failed requests |
| Minimum Response Time | Lowest response time |
| Maximum Response Time | Highest response time |

**Expected output format:**

```text
Test Plan: ARMS Homepage Load Test
Target Users: 500
Ramp-up Period: 100 seconds

Average Response Time: Recorded by JMeter
Throughput: Recorded by JMeter
Error Rate: Recorded by JMeter
Minimum Response Time: Recorded by JMeter
Maximum Response Time: Recorded by JMeter

Load Test Completed.
```

## RESULT
Thus, load testing of the ARMS homepage was designed using Apache JMeter with 500 simulated concurrent users. Response time, throughput, and error rate can be analyzed using the JMeter reports.
